Template: truenas-proxmox-plugin/setup-multipath
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Install the TrueNAS multipath profile?
 The plugin ships a device{} profile for TrueNAS iSCSI targets with the
 vendor's recommended settings: ALUA hardware handler, immediate failback,
 no_path_retry queue, fast_io_fail_tmo 10, dev_loss_tmo 30. These values
 hold a path down across a TrueNAS HA failover (~20-60 s) without failing
 I/O out.
 .
 Answering yes installs this profile at
 /etc/multipath/conf.d/truenas-proxmox-plugin.conf and asks multipathd to
 reload its configuration. Future plugin upgrades keep the profile in
 sync. You can change your mind later with
 'dpkg-reconfigure truenas-proxmox-plugin'.
 .
 Answer no if you manage /etc/multipath.conf yourself, if this node does
 not use iSCSI (NVMe/TCP only), or if you want to try the plugin without
 touching system-wide multipath configuration. The plugin itself does
 not require the profile to function; the profile only changes how
 dm-multipath merges TrueNAS iSCSI paths.
